$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General experimental procedure for the
preparation of oxazole or isoxazole-3-carboxylic acid coupled amino acids
(1-9): To a solution of 5-methylisoxazole-3-carboxylic acid (0.5 g, 3.94
mmol)) in dichloromethane (DCM) (16 ml, 0.25 M) was added triethylamine
(TEA) (1.13 ml, 7.88 mmol), EDC.HCl (0.91 g, 4.73 mmol) and HOBT (0.53 g,
3.94 mmol) at 0 oC. After stirring the reaction mixture for 5 min, the
amino acid methyl ester hydrochloride (0.72 g, 4.73 mmol) was added. Then
the reaction mixture was bringing to room temperature and stir for
overnight. Water was added and the mixture was extracted with ethyl
acetate. The combined organic layers were washed with brine and dried
over anhydrous sodium sulfate and concentrated in vacuo. The resulting
residue was purified by silica gel flash column chromatography to afford
the desired product. (S)-Methyl 2-(5-methylisoxazole-3-carboxamido)
butanoate (1): According to the general experimental procedure, compound
1 was prepared from methyl ester of (L) 2-aminobutyric acid
(H-Abu-OMe.HCl). (2S, 3R)-Methyl
3-tert-butoxy-2-(5-methylisoxazole-3-carboxamido) butanoate (7):
According to the general experimental procedure, compound 7 was prepared
for methyl ester of (L) Threonine (L-H-Thr-OMe.HCl). As colorless solid
in 0.84 g (72% yield). R f = 0.30 in hexane/ethyl acetate = 3/1. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.45 (d, J = 9.0 Hz, 1H), 6.41 (s, 1H), 4.62 (dd, J =
9.2, 1.9 Hz, 1H), 4.31-4.26 (m, 1H), 3.71 (s, 3H), 2.47 (s, 3H), 1.21 (t,
J = 6.3 Hz, 3H), 1.12 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 171.1, 170.7,
159.6, 158.4, 101.5, 74.2, 67.4, 57.9, 57.9, 52.3, 28.3, 21.0, 12.3.
HRMS: calculated for C14H22N2O5Na [M+Na+]: 321.1424; found: 321.1426.
